k rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weakened-us-fuel-efficiency-rules-and-promises-of-cheaper-cars-could-see-drivers-pay-higher-running-costs-while-also-increasing-carbon-emissions/a-79496554?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Weakened US fuel-efficiency rules and promises of cheaper cars could yet see drivers pay higher running costs while increasing planet-heating emissions.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UAE launches Flydubai hijacking and terrorism investigation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efa0de99c622b3b2d036087e5afe12fdc7b22e38bb0e33a13f0a061433760b61</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T10:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uae-launches-flydubai-hijacking-and-terrorism-investigation/a-79497746--17ff1e197de5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uae-launches-flydubai-hijacking-and-terrorism-investigation/a-79497746?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UAE's chief prosecutor said it's looking at the possibility of "terrorist activity or intent" in the alleged attempted hijacking of a Flydubai commercial flight to Tel Aviv. It says it has jurisdiction in the case.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germans' biggest fear is the high cost of living, an annual study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6924d5f05b2abccfbc3cef939d7410caaa7c2f93e8b567ce3cb68be808ff3e31</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762--40495e454721.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germans-biggest-fear-is-the-high-cost-of-living-an-annual-study-finds/a-79497762?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What do Germans fear most in 2026? Wars? Global crises? Wrong. Their biggest concern is the cost of living, which keeps rising.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan launches deadly airstrikes on Afghanistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8aeea4d3f5d6fc11595984b0d4f340d92eff247f16500b05e3af056b8be60d9d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T09:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-launches-deadly-airstrikes-on-afghanistan/a-79498092--42bd1620b7f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-launches-deadly-airstrikes-on-afghanistan/a-79498092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Taliban government in Afghanistan said at least nine civilians were killed in Pakistani airstrikes on two provinces overnight. Pakistan said it had struck militant hideouts, killing 22 fighters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Cristiano Ronaldo walks out of Portugal camp</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54ee874b70d5b1d6427f7ef743962b3de8ed952f6f87f1ff9af0ecd05611c538</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T08:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-walks-out-of-portugal-camp/a-79497238--be4e02847569.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cristiano-ronaldo-walks-out-of-portugal-camp/a-79497238?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cristiano Ronaldo has left Portugal’s camp after learning that he would not start the next Nations League match. Portugal's coach has denied reports of a rift between himself and the star player.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee halts woman's execution after 'failed' attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd62ae513829c441788003726ab3e2f809f298c6156cf2e3fc8974e8947f7b7f</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T07:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennessee-halts-woman-s-execution-after-failed-attempt/a-79496561--90352fa2ac40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennessee-halts-woman-s-execution-after-failed-attempt/a-79496561?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike was found alive and snoring, despite being administered two injections of a lethal drug. The state governor has ordered a review of the botched execution.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin leftists seek to pave way for coalition</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b09154b7da419ee26b53796537c887b324f717143d89b14e79cb9a3245a132d</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:32:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-leftists-seek-to-pave-way-for-coalition/live-79496180--ffa005d1dac5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-leftists-seek-to-pave-way-for-coalition/live-79496180?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Berlin Left Party, Greens and SPD are to meet to clarify controversial issues ahead of possible coalition talks. The second fuel tax cut this year has come into force as gas and diesel prices spiral. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Swiss glaciers lose more than 5% in ice volume in 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2526affc1583fb699d7700ed5dd21c68638a7e0268d4756da4f05a73a2c75a9c</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T03:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-in-ice-volume-in-2026/a-79495965--ebd2291f40e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-in-ice-volume-in-2026/a-79495965?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the last five years, Swiss glaciers have lost nearly 20% of their mass, and 2026 saw the second-biggest loss of glacier volume on record. Experts warn there could be no ice left in the next 10-15 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US military cuts generals, admirals by 20%, Hegseth says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5aea675a20d508b04ba2346e1684a04fd34e76dcdfdff3d857895d0a036f547</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T01:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-military-cuts-generals-admirals-by-20-hegseth-says/a-79495683--79e31e8a192e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-military-cuts-generals-admirals-by-20-hegseth-says/a-79495683?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US defense secretary has also unveiled major changes, including a new drone command and an Elon Musk-led task force to assess the future of warfare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested as student protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26c1f51b1e28c3ee8efe1e72a7ecbc8131e039eedecaefc0595366f8d1aa2286</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633--b363f8aabae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Student protests have grown in scale and intensity, with violent clashes in some places leading to hundreds of arrests and dozens of injuries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: NGO reports dire camp conditions, says Israel is moving 'Yellow Line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b2dc517da4391888d73c4fc745f926d4864142010ef319e8732478476b7e297</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777--aae790bffc81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Danish Refugee Council alleges that Israel is employing "a policy of protracted displacement" in Gaza. It says the so-called "Yellow Line" is creeping west toward the coast, preventing many from returning home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f90e415f1dd81db3d3ff71acb0bea9b09d2bfba8538692928a6242c6e4ac096</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai pilot investigated over possible attempt to crash Tel Aviv-bound flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed522859fb4dbe428887eadb150e89b69fdc03236ca771dfc4660ca114da98a8</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761--24ed602fb272.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Flydubai service from the UAE to Israel made an emergency landing after the copilot stabbed the captain. Eyewitnesses said he attempted to crash the plane before he was subdued by passengers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France, Spain welcome idea of UK rejoining EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:737967385f0e30777e7277b76eeaa460f2d3c7438f827af4514a127e8e22c855</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:33:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-spain-s-sanchez-welcome-idea-of-uk-rejoining-eu-after-burnham-remarks/a-79493469--0632af9b0576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-spain-welcome-idea-of-uk-rejoining-eu/a-79493469?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Spain, France's Emmanuel Macron said it would be "good news" if the UK moves towards the EU, with Pedro Sanchez also embracing the idea. UK PM Andy Burnham has not ruled out rejoining the bloc.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Are the Houthis winning against Saudi Arabia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:107f9549aaebbe3b447ced5dc477ffaf62465d837bdb296b59198ae4a0289e5e</id><updated>2026-10-01T15:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476--c9910a2a90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's unclear how the Saudis can defuse the threat presented by the Houthis in next-door Yemen or who they can turn to for help. The US isn't interested, the Europeans are hedging and nobody wants open conflict with Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
